# Decrypted output and cluster credentials — never committed
*.dec.yaml
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig

# NOTE: this file deliberately does NOT ignore `*-secret.yaml`.
#
# ExternalSecret manifests are conventionally named `<app>-secret.yaml`, because
# they produce a Secret of that name. Ignoring that pattern would silently drop
# legitimate, secret-free manifests: `git add -A` would not stage them, `git status`
# would not mention them, and Argo CD would never reconcile them — with no error
# anywhere to explain why the app was missing its configuration.
#
# A filename tells you nothing about whether a manifest carries key material.
# That question is answered by scripts/no-plaintext-secrets.py, which parses the
# YAML and inspects the actual fields.
